   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend a chapter of the laws of 2020 relating to requiring the\ndepartment of labor to produce a report regarding summer youth employment\nprograms funded by state, federal and local appropriations, as proposed in\nlegislative bills numbers S. 1079 and A. 6393, in relation to requiring the\noffice of temporary and disability assistance to produce a report regarding\nthe summer youth employment program and to the effectiveness of the provisions\nthereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S1300",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S1300-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§1, 2 & 3, Chap of 2020 (as proposed in S.1079 & A.6393)",
    "lawSection": "Labor",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S1300\n\nSPONSOR: PERSAUD\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend a chapter of the laws of 2020 relating to requiring the\ndepartment of labor to produce a report regarding summer youth employ-\nment programs funded by state, federal and local appropriations, as\nproposed in legislative bills numbers S. 1079 and A. 6393, in relation\nto requiring the office of temporary and disability assistance to\nproduce a report regarding the summer youth employment program and to\nthe effectiveness of the provisions thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to amend Chapter 297 of the Laws of 2020 in\norder to refine the parameters for a report regarding the Summer Youth\nEmployment Program.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of this bill would require. the New York State Office of\nTemporary and Disability Assistance, in consultation with the Department\nof Labor, State Education Department, and the Office of Children and\nFamily Services, to produce a report on the Summer Youth Employment\nProgram by May 1, 2022. It would also limit the lookback period for\ncertain criteria to be included in such report, covering the years from\n2016 to 2021.\n\nSection two of this bill would amend the effective date of the original\nlegislation from one year to two years after enactment.\n\nSection three of this bill would establish the effective date.\n\n \nDIFFERENCE BETWEEN ORIGINAL AND AMENDED VERSION (IF APPLICABLE):\n\nN/A\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Summer Youth Employment Program provides critical opportunities for\nat-risk youth across the state to learn valuable skills and discover new\ninterests in their communities. Through this program, individuals\nbetween the ages of and 14 and 24 are eligible to receive paid summer\njobs at various employment sites within government, nonprofit, public\nservice, and the private sector.\n\nThese programs help provide critical educational and job training oppor-\ntunities, enhance resumes, and important assistance to at-risk popu-\nlations.\n\nChapter 297 of the Laws of 2020 requires the New York State Department\nof Labor, the State Education Department, the Office of Temporary and\nDisability Assistance, and the Office of Children and Families to\nprepare a report studying current practices within the Summer Youth\nEmployment Program in order to provide guidance on best practices, job\nopportunities, and places for improvement. This bill would refine the\nparameters of such reporting requirements in recognition of the substan-\ntial amount of information to be collected by the agencies, as well as\nthe challenges presented by the COVID-19 pandemic on the 2020 and 2021\nprograms.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately; provided, however, that section\none of this act shall take effect on the same date and in the same\nmanner as a chapter of the laws of 2020 relating to requiring the\ndepartment of labor to produce a report regarding summer youth employ-\nment programs funded by state, federal and local appropriations, as\nproposed in legislative bills numbers S.1079 and A.6393, takes effect.\n",
